# Sample files

A sample of each file kind the parsers read, `<file_kind>/<case>.<ext>`: a small real
file, the first rows of one as conventions §10 allows, or, where the file is over the
256 KiB cap and its format cannot be cut by bytes, one that a script writes from one
download in the file's own form; never typed in by hand (sdk-core ADR-0020). A binary file
carries no comment, so each sample's provenance is one row here: the release id, the URL,
the bytes and sha256 of the full file as upstream serves it, the UTC time it was fetched,
with `Z`, and under Kept what of the file the sample keeps, such as the whole file, its
first rows, or the sheets and cells the tests read.

